WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.580
Maybe the worst part though,

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.920
was his laughter as he contorted himself,

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:14.000
to where his torso was now outstretched into the room with me,

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.560
and his arms were wildly waving in my direction.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:25.300
Hello, and welcome to Al Dente Creepypasta,
horror stories cooked to perfection with a

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:32.981
splash of red sauce. My name is CZ and I will
be your server this episode. Today’s episode

00:00:32.981 --> 00:00:38.420
is a sequel to Creepy Clown School Lockdown,
which you can click or tap here to listen

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.940
to if you wish, but you don’t necessarily
have to watch them in order. This time we’re

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.399
moving up to high school. I know many of you
don’t look back at your high school years

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.829
too fondly, but I think today’s offering
will make you appreciate your experience a

00:00:52.829 --> 00:01:00.170
little bit more. Let’s dig right in.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.340
Fourth period Algebra was the most dreaded
part of my day. Not only do I hate math, but

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:10.020
it's the last morning class before lunch.
The schedule gets a little easier once I hit

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.850
that afternoon hump, but that hump is a big
one. I've never been good with math, and having

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:21.640
Mrs. Nelson, or as we call her, the Crypt
Keeper, was NOT making things easier this

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:26.580
semester. In fact, the only thing keeping
me afloat in that class was the fact that

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.320
my friends Chris was texting me the answers
from 2nd period.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.570
It was a muggy afternoon towards the end of
the school year. As usual, Mrs. Nelson refused

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:40.800
to turn on the air conditioning. It was somehow
fitting to be broiling through my 4th period

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.800
hell.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.790
We started the Thursday exam and The Crypt
Keeper plopped behind her desk in the front

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.540
corner of the room. Idiot. Cheating my way
though this would be easier that I thought.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:54.430
I placed down a water bottle and slyly slid
my phone across my desk into the bottle's

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.710
shadow. Piece of cake. I opened up the text
conversation with Chris and began to transfer

00:01:59.710 --> 00:02:08.500
the information onto the page. A. B. A. 24.3
repeating. I had to mix in a couple wrong

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.800
answers as well, just to make it believable.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:17.439
Just then, I hear the unmistakable sound...
someone getting up from a chair. My eyes dart

00:02:17.439 --> 00:02:22.900
up and see the old pile of bones rising to
her feet. Crap. I wondered if she suspected

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.870
something. She began to pace towards my desk.
Just my luck... I guess I'd have to act like

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:32.519
I was actually trying to solve the equations
until she sat back down. It was like reading

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:38.290
another language. I had no idea what I was
doing. That's when I noticed my phone buzz.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.150
I should have turned off the vibration before
the test. I don't think it gave me away though.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:48.159
Could have been anyone's phone from anyone's
pocket. But there was bad news. The vibration

00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:52.420
started sliding my phone down the small incline
of the desk. It slowly slid away from the

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:56.530
safe cover of the water bottle. I glanced
up to the teacher. Her eyes were locked on

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.590
to me. The phone continued to slide down.
All I could do was hope that it stopped, or

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:05.390
that she'd turn away long enough for me to
slip the phone into my pocket. No such luck.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.120
It fell off the desk and onto the floor. Trying
to play it off like it had fallen out of my

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:15.150
pocket, I reached down to grab the phone.
But a cold, bony hand grasped my wrist before

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.590
I could.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:23.629
"Office. Now." Those were the only words that
came out of her mouth.

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:28.080
At least it was air-conditioned in the area
outside the Dean's office where I sat to await

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.700
my sentencing. The Dean's office was a smaller
room within the confines of the main office,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:37.930
which basically connects all the offices of
the administration, who were supposedly all

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:42.109
out at lunch, so I'd have to wait for the
Dean to return before I would find out how

00:03:42.109 --> 00:03:44.560
long I'd be spending in detention.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:50.200
You can imagine my surprise when a fully costumed
circus clown dragging a big hammer, walked

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:55.700
into the room with me. That seemed odd. I
hadn't heard of any assemblies or anything

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.280
going on this week.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:03.010
I'm not exactly sure when I had the realization
that something foul was up with this clown.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.340
It wasn't when he grabbed a chair and shoved
it under the main door of the office to jam

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.510
it shut. I just saw it as more of a gag to
try to get me to crack a smile for some reason.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:16.510
I guess when it started to get a bit uncomfortable
was when he dragged his hammer across the

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:21.340
desks in the middle of the office, knocking
over a bunch of stuff and making a mess, all

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:27.140
while locking eye contact with me and giggling
maniacally. Still, I just had no reason to

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:32.400
get too freaked out any further than bit of
nervous laughter. I mean, for all I knew the

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.210
school's admin could have been pranking each
other.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:40.800
No, I don't think it was until I saw the clown
start talking to himself when the panic started

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.800
to set in.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:49.190
"He-HA! Step right up and test your might!"

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:54.020
Then he swung the hammer in the air, high
over his head and freaking smashed it down

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.590
on the doorknob to the Principal's office!
The door was basically destroyed and swung

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:02.930
right open. Then the clown looked at me, dead
in the eyes and said:

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:06.810
"Ho-ho! Look's like we've got a winner!"

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:12.230
Then he trudged into the Principal's office.
I was frozen in fear at this point, not sure

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:16.500
if I should run for it and find someone, or
if I was on a hidden camera show or what the

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.940
hell was going on.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:22.370
Meanwhile, the clown was rummaging around
in the Principal's office when I heard...

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:30.820
a loud crack from the school's intercom system.followed
by the sound of analog feedback. It went on

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:37.770
for a few seconds before being replaced by...
circus music, but it sounded creepy and messed

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:42.340
up. I think he had blown out the speaker on
the intercom. I also felt the air-conditioner

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.250
come to a halt, and if I wasn't mistaken,
it had been replaced with heat.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.800
The clown side-shuffled out of the Principal's
office with his hammer slung over the shoulder

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:56.700
and the most evil-looking sinister grin. What
was shocking about his appearance was how

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:01.550
wide his smile spread. It looked like his
grin nearly stretched from ear to ear, and

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:07.390
I mean that literally. That, and the glowing
look in his eyes told me I needed to bolt,

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:12.080
right now! I sprang out of my chair just as
the clown screeched and charged at me! I slipped

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.120
into the Dean's office before he could get
to me, slammed the door and locked it. I knew

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.160
that wouldn't cover me for long though, so
I immediately went to the desk and tried to

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.870
push it in front of the door. It was much
heavier than it looked. I couldn't get the

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:27.310
thing to budge! The bookshelf would have to
do for now, but I knew I was only biding my

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:28.310
time.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:32.480
I felt the crash of the hammer's impact attack
the door as I positioned the bookshelf. It

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.500
not only knocked the doorknob off, but smashed
the wood in in the area all around the doorknob,

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.770
letting in a beam of light from the outside.
That light soon became blotted out by the

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:47.810
clown's huge yellow smile staring at me through
the hole. He began to cackle. I didn't know

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:52.370
how long I had. I instinctively reached for
my phone to try to call for help... but my

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:57.560
I felt my heart plunge as I realized that
it had been confiscated by Mrs. Nelson. I

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.500
looked around the tiny office. There was a
phone on the desk -- a landline. I picked

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:06.610
it up and punched 9-1-1, but as soon as I
brought it to my ear, all I got was signal.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.950
The line had somehow been disconnected.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:14.260
With no window in the room, I had no means
of escape. And with the main office door barricaded,

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:21.550
I was trapped in here with this.... this maniac.
Just then I realized he was no longer staring

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:26.410
through the hole. He was going to try to ram
it in again. I felt my eyes well up with tears

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:31.780
as I started to realize all the possibilities
of what he might do to me. With one last ditch

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:35.740
effort, I grunted and pushed the Dean's desk
as hard as I could, and managed to tip it

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:39.750
over and send it slamming to the ground! The
picture of the Dean's daughter shattered on

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.550
the floor, but there was no time to worry
about the repercussions of that now. The door

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:47.801
was starting to open and I was able to drive
the desk just far enough to stop the clown

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:48.801
from getting in!

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:53.550
I struggled to push the desk for a few moments
more, and it seemed like we were at a stalemate.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:59.320
Then it seemed like the he had stopped pushing.the
sound of the circus music abruptly stopped,

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:05.180
and as far as I could tell like the clown
had given up. Then, out of nowhere, through

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:09.360
the partially open and partially busted door,
the clown lodged himself in the opening and

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:13.690
tried to squeeze himself through. I screamed
when I saw the circus makeup melting off his

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:19.610
face like some kind of nightmarish Munch painting.
His once round puffy red wig was now drenched

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:25.860
in sweat and stuck to his face in a series
of dark red strands.Maybe the worst part through,

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.090
was his laughter as he contorted himself to
where his torso was outstretched into the

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.650
room with me and his arms wildly waved in
my direction.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:38.180
Instinctively, I jumped back, which was a
bad idea, because he was then able to retract

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:43.240
back to the other side of what was left of
the door and slowly but surely force it open

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:48.330
in my direction. At this point he'd surely
get in. All I could do was prepare myself

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.990
to fight a battle I knew I could not win.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:57.310
Then... out of nowhere, his progress just
stopped... This time I didn't let down my

00:08:57.310 --> 00:09:01.811
guard. I stood on high alert when I noticed
some banging around in the background. Someone

00:09:01.811 --> 00:09:05.350
was trying to get into the office! I suddenly
could see the light at the end of the tunnel

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:07.079
and hoped I might be saved.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:10.800
The main office door was kicked down and the
voice of the school police officer yelled

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:11.820
out!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:17.290
"Freeze! Get your hands in the air!" I have
to admit, it didn't sound very convincing

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.560
given that I could hear the tremble in his
voice. But I was at least somewhat comforted

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.420
knowing he'd be armed.

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:28.090
I called out for help and the officer rushed
to my aid. The strange part was, the clown

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:33.230
was nowhere to be found. I explained that
he had smashed in this door moments before,

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:37.410
but in searching the entire office, we couldn't
figure out how he had gotten away.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:41.950
All in fact, there were only two pieces of
evidence that ended up being found. One was

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:46.220
a rubber clown nose left clamped on the microphone
in the Principal's office that was hooked

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:51.610
up the school's PA system. The other was a
knot of red hair from the clown's wig. I would

00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:57.230
later find out that they ran tests on it and
discovered that it was real human hair. It

00:09:57.230 --> 00:10:02.430
belonged to this guy Bronson, who was currently
in prison serving a 15 year sentence. There

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:07.060
was no way he had escaped, so the appearance
of his DNA only added to the mystery...

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:11.579
I wish I could say it ended there... with
me getting out of my punishment on account

00:10:11.579 --> 00:10:15.540
of the traumatic experience, but there was
one more haunting thing that happened.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:21.430
While it was true I didn't have to serve my
detention, I think it's safe to say that I

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:26.730
learned my lesson, and I was never going to
cheat on another test again, or do anything

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.410
that might get my phone confiscated for that
matter. I was able to scratch by and pass

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:36.519
math class with a D. My parents weren't happy
about it, but again, I got a little sympathy

00:10:36.519 --> 00:10:40.740
after having nearly become the jester's afternoon
snack or whatever.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:45.240
So summer came and I was free for a couple
more months. Chris and I were skateboarding

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:50.350
on the street toward 7/11 and I heard a strange
sound and stopped.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:55.920
"What's wrong?" Chris asked me. I held up
an index finger. I listened for a moment,

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:01.791
and I was sure I could make out the sound
of... the same circus music from that day

00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:07.990
in the office. I looked up to find the car
it was coming from, a beat up red bug, no

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:14.300
license plate. My eyes met with the driver's:
it was the same very same clown from before,

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:19.449
again with the makeup melted down off his
face onto his collar in a most disturbing

00:11:19.449 --> 00:11:29.139
manner. He rolled up the window.

